      </Style>
      <Point>
        <coordinates>-77.03510206062472,38.88976840124993,38.37403692473739</coordinates>
      </Point>
    </Placemark>
    <Placemark>
      <description>Basilica of the National Shrine of the Immaculate Conception 
4th Street &amp; Michigan Avenue NE 
Washington, DC
Height 100 m 329 ft 
Facts 
- The National Shrine is the largest Roman Catholic church in the Western Hemisphere and the eighth largest in the world. It measures a total of 459 feet long and covers an area of 77,500 square feet.  
- Largest Roman Catholic church in the United States.  
- The tower is called &quot;Knights&apos; Tower&quot; because it was built with a donation from the Knights of Columbus.  
- The National Shrine contains Pope Paul VI&apos;s coronation tiara, of which he relinquished shortly after assuming the role of pope.</description>
      <name>2.) Basilica of the National Shrine</name>
      <View>
        <longitude>-77.00070915905559</longitude>
        <latitude>38.93290765347393</latitude>
        <range>173.6970177617028</range>
