      </Point>
    </Placemark>
    <Placemark>
      <description>United States Capitol	
Washington, DC
Height - 88 m 288 ft 
- The United States Capitol was originally designed by Dr. William Thornton, an amateur architect, who submitted a plan in 1793 that won him $500 and a city lot.  
- The present Capitol was designed and constructed by Thomas U. Walter, 4th architect of the Capitol.  
- Today&apos;s cast iron dome at its greatest exterior measures 135 ft. 5 in., and is topped by the bronze Statue of Freedom that stands 19.5 ft. and weighs 14,985 lbs.</description>
      <name>5) United States Capitol</name>
      <View>
