    <Placemark>
      <description>1100 Pennsylvania Avenue NW
Washington, DC
Height - 96 m 315 ft 
- The 10 &quot;Congress Bells&quot; in the tower are rung for 3½ hrs at the opening and closing of Congress, and for state occasions.  
- The tower has a free public observatory.  
- The building was nearly demolished in 1971, but was saved by the efforts of Nancy Hanks and a preservation organization.  
- The Old Post Office Building was designated a National Historic Landmark in 1973 and a National Park Site on February 15, 1983</description>
      <name>3) Old Post Office Building</name>
